WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.720
Speaker 1: Welcome to the David Pakman&nbsp;
show. I am Ferron Cousins from Ring of Fire,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:09.360
sitting in once again today for David Pakman.&nbsp;
We've got a wonderful show coming up for you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:17.100
today. Jim Jordan is being sued by Alvin Bragg.&nbsp;
Melania Trump is furious at the media for talking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:22.140
about all of her marriage problems. Dianne&nbsp;
Feinstein is facing more and more calls to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:27.900
resign after it was revealed that she has missed&nbsp;
more than 60 votes this year. And, of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:36.240
all the legal problems with Donald Trump. All of&nbsp;
that and more is coming up on today's program. So&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:43.560
let's jump right into it. Alvin Bragg, Manhattan&nbsp;
district attorney, has announced that he is suing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:50.640
Republican Representative Jim Jordan and pretty&nbsp;
much the House Judiciary Committee trying to stop&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.640 --> 00:01:00.960
a subpoena that Jordan issued last week. For Mark&nbsp;
Pomeranz. Now, I had already thought that the idea&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:08.700
to subpoena Mark Pomeranz by Jim Jordan was very&nbsp;
dumb. If you're not familiar with Mark Pomeranz,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:13.980
he is one of the two former assistant&nbsp;
prosecutors at the Manhattan DA's office,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.980 --> 00:01:21.840
along with Kerry Dunn. They worked under Cyrus&nbsp;
Vance on the Trump investigation and Pomeranz and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:28.260
Dunn resigned last year. And Pomeranz has revealed&nbsp;
since then in both his resignation letter and his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.260 --> 00:01:35.700
new book that he resigned because when Alvin Bragg&nbsp;
took over from Cy Vance, he pretty much killed the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:45.240
investigation into Donald Trump. Pomeranz has gone&nbsp;
as far as to say that he and Vance actually had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:52.260
the indictments drafted against Donald Trump.&nbsp;
He said they were less than ten days away from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.260 --> 00:01:59.160
charging Donald Trump with financial crimes. And&nbsp;
then Brad came in, put that investigation on ice,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:04.860
and the rest is history, right? Well, Jim Jordan,&nbsp;
for some reason thought it would be a smart idea&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:11.460
to bring Pomeranz into the House Judiciary&nbsp;
Committee to testify because he thought&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:17.880
Pomeranz his testimony would somehow prove&nbsp;
that Alvin Bragg had actually weaponized.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:27.360
The Manhattan DA's office to go after Trump&nbsp;
and he weaponized it to go after Trump by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:34.440
not going after Trump, according to the guy&nbsp;
Jim Jordan wants to talk to in the House. So&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:42.540
if it's a little confusing, don't worry. It's very&nbsp;
confusing. Jim Jordan's strategy here makes no&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:48.660
sense at all. Pomeranz is not going to waltz into&nbsp;
the House Judiciary Committee and say, Oh yeah,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:54.420
Alvin Bragg Absolutely weaponize this. No, he is&nbsp;
going to say, based on what he's already said,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.420 --> 00:02:58.500
that Alvin Bragg should have gone harder&nbsp;
after Donald Trump, and then he's going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.500 --> 00:03:03.480
to start laying out all the evidence they had&nbsp;
against Donald Trump with the financial crimes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.440 --> 00:03:11.100
So if Pomeranz goes to that Judiciary Committee&nbsp;
hearing, it's going to make Jim Jordan look even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.100 --> 00:03:16.740
dumber than he already has this year. I think&nbsp;
that's a good thing. I want that to happen.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.640 --> 00:03:25.200
But I can understand why Alvin Bragg doesn't. And&nbsp;
that, of course, is why Alvin Bragg is suing to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:30.840
stop this subpoena from happening. And honestly,&nbsp;
legally speaking, he has very strong grounds under&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.840 --> 00:03:36.480
which to challenge this subpoena. He can easily&nbsp;
say that, obviously, because these are ongoing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:42.420
investigations, they have not been closed.&nbsp;
We, under New York state law, are forbidden&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.420 --> 00:03:46.980
from turning over evidence, from turning over&nbsp;
documents related to ongoing investigations&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.980 --> 00:03:51.960
to third parties. And at this point, because&nbsp;
Congress does not directly oversee the Manhattan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:56.940
DA's office, they would be considered a third&nbsp;
party. It'd be no different than handing over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.940 --> 00:04:02.820
the information that they've gathered to Fox News.&nbsp;
That's kind of how Congress is for the Manhattan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.820 --> 00:04:06.960
DA's office. You're just an independent&nbsp;
third party. Sure, you've got some power,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:14.940
but you have no power here. So he has very&nbsp;
strong legal grounds under which to challenge&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:23.520
this subpoena. But I kind of wish he wouldn't.&nbsp;
I really, really, really want Mark Pomerantz to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.520 --> 00:04:31.380
waltz into that chamber and spill the beans on&nbsp;
all of the horrible evidence that they uncovered&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.380 --> 00:04:36.240
in their Trump investigation. That is what I want&nbsp;
to see. And I think a lot of people probably want&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.240 --> 00:04:41.820
to see that as well. If we're going to air some&nbsp;
dirty laundry, let's air it out. Let's put it all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.820 --> 00:04:47.820
out there on the line for the world to see,&nbsp;
because that's what Jim Jordan wants to do.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:53.940
And I think in this particular instance, we need&nbsp;
to honor Jim Jordan's request. We need to give&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.940 --> 00:05:01.500
him exactly what he wants. Because I believe, as&nbsp;
Oscar Wilde has said, you know, there's two great&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:08.700
tragedies in life. One is not getting what you&nbsp;
want. The other is getting exactly what you want.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.960 --> 00:05:16.740
So let's give Jim Jordan exactly what&nbsp;
he wants. Let's give him Marc Pomerantz,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.740 --> 00:05:23.880
his testimony about the investigations into Donald&nbsp;
Trump. Let's let the entire country hear what Mark&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:29.940
Pomerantz has to say about all of that evidence,&nbsp;
about the indictments that they had drafted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.780 --> 00:05:38.760
and about why those indictments didn't get filed.&nbsp;
Let's hear it from him. But that's not what Jim&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.760 --> 00:05:44.100
Jordan wants to hear. It's what he would hear,&nbsp;
but it's not what he wants to hear. He wants to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.100 --> 00:05:49.620
hear. Pomeranz Go in there and whine and cry&nbsp;
and say, Oh, Alvin Bragg made us look at this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.620 --> 00:05:54.720
stuff and we didn't want to. We knew it was phony&nbsp;
baloney. But yeah, that ain't going to happen.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.000 --> 00:06:02.400
But flip side of the coin, as I said, I&nbsp;
understand why Bragg doesn't want this to happen.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.180 --> 00:06:08.640
If Pomeranz were to go into a Judiciary&nbsp;
Committee hearing and start saying that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.640 --> 00:06:13.140
Bragg was a weak prosecutor, we had all this&nbsp;
strong evidence. He chose not to do it. It's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.140 --> 00:06:17.040
going to make Bragg look bad, and then you're&nbsp;
going to have people on the left as well as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.040 --> 00:06:23.100
all of the freaks on the right hating on Alvin&nbsp;
Bragg. And that's not what we need right now.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.060 --> 00:06:30.840
I am still annoyed. I'm still angry that Alvin&nbsp;
Bragg did not go after Donald Trump for the big&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.840 --> 00:06:36.120
financial crimes that Pomerantz and Don and Vance&nbsp;
were all investigating and ready to indict him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.120 --> 00:06:41.700
for. I think that was a mistake. I think that&nbsp;
was a giant misstep based on the statements&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:41.700 --> 00:06:46.440
that Pomerantz has already made publicly. It&nbsp;
seems very clear that they had Donald Trump&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.440 --> 00:06:52.500
red handed in a lot of these instances. Now,&nbsp;
that would have been up for a jury to decide.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.460 --> 00:06:58.740
But now a jury is not even going to get the&nbsp;
opportunity to decide that. And that's not fair.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.580 --> 00:07:04.920
If the indictments were ready, as Pomerantz&nbsp;
says they were, they should have been filed.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.480 --> 00:07:12.480
Bragg didn't want to go that route. Bragg went the&nbsp;
route he did. He got his indictments, you know,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.480 --> 00:07:19.320
34 counts against Donald Trump. Trial coming up&nbsp;
probably in about a year. So it all worked itself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:19.320 --> 00:07:25.500
out. But Bragg doesn't want Pomerantz to talk.&nbsp;
And again, I understand why and I understand&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.500 --> 00:07:29.760
there's laws in New York that would likely&nbsp;
prevent Pomerantz from saying the things that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.760 --> 00:07:39.480
I want to hear him say. But. Bragg has the law&nbsp;
on his side. Jim Jordan only has politicization,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:39.480 --> 00:07:48.120
the weaponization of the weaponization committee.&nbsp;
And maybe he wins. Maybe he doesn't. We'll see&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.120 --> 00:07:52.860
what happens. As this lawsuit that Bragg has&nbsp;
filed plays itself out in the court system

